.\" Man page for ncdu-next
.TH NCNEXT 1 "2026-10-22" "ncdu-next 1.0" "ncdu-next manual"
.SH NAME
ncdu-next \- modern disk-usage analyzer with TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncdu-next
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ncdu-next scans a directory tree and displays disk usage in a terminal user
interface. By default it does not follow symlinks, counts hardlinked file size
once, and crosses filesystems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--path DIR
Root directory to scan (default: current directory).
.TP
.B \--workers N
Number of parallel scan workers (default: 4).
.TP
.B \--exclude PATTERN
Skip entries whose name matches the glob \fIPATTERN\fR. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \--one-file-system
Do not descend into other filesystems / mount points. Implemented on Linux,
macOS and Windows; when the filesystem identity cannot be read the flag fails
open (it warns and crosses mount points rather than hiding data).
.TP
.B \--count-hardlinks
Count the size of every hardlink separately instead of once per inode.
.TP
.B \--follow-symlinks
Follow symbolic links (cycle guarded).
.TP
.B \--trash
Send deletions to OS trash instead of permanent deletion.
.TP
.B \--export FILE
Write ncdu 2.x JSON tree to \fIFILE\fR and exit without opening the TUI.
.TP
.B \--debuginfo FILE
Write a debuginfo zip bundle to \fIFILE\fR and exit without opening the TUI. May
be combined with \fI\-\-export\fR and does not require \fI\-\-debug\fR.
.TP
.B \--debuginfo-tree
Include the full file list (\fItree.jsonl\fR) in the debuginfo bundle. Ignored
with a warning when \fI\-\-debuginfo\fR is not set.
.TP
.B \--version
Print the binary's build identity (module version, embedded revision, toolchain,
platform) and exit. The information is read from the binary itself, so it needs
no config file and no VCS checkout; a build with no revision stamp says so.
.TP
.B \--json
With \fI\-\-version\fR, print the same information as machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B \--config FILE
Load TOML config from \fIFILE\fR (command-line flags override).
.TP
.B \--detect-format
Populate the encoding and line-ending fields on text-like files.
.TP
.B \--debug
Enable the in-program Debug tab (see the D key).
.TP
.B \-v, \--verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Show this help and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B \e, Ctrl-C
Quit.
.TP
.B Up / k
Select previous entry.
.TP
.B Down / j
Select next entry.
.TP
.B Enter / l
Open selected directory.
.TP
.B Backspace / h
Go to parent directory.
.TP
.B e, w
Toggle the wide view. Simple shows the name and size; wide adds the broad kind,
Windows file attributes, specific type id, encoding/line-ending, and modification
time. On a terminal narrower than about 120 columns each wide record is shown
across two lines rather than being cut off.
.TP
.B u
Cycle the size unit: bytes, then 1024-based IEC (KiB, MiB, GiB, ...), then
1000-based SI (kB, MB, GB, ...). All modes are integer-only.
.TP
.B /
Open the live filter prompt for the current directory. Typing filters the rows
as you type; Enter applies and closes the prompt; Tab toggles deep (recursive)
scope; Esc clears the filter.
.TP
.B f
Toggle deep (recursive) scope on the committed filter.
.TP
.B g
Open the full-tree search prompt. Enter runs it and shows a flat, user-navigable
results list; Enter on a result jumps to it; Esc closes.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the active filter, or close the search results.
.TP
.B D
Open the read-only Debug tab (requires \-\-debug). It has a \fBtab\fR zone (the
inspected tab's detail and its filesystem section) and a \fBprogram\fR zone
(runtime counters, totals, and the record reference). While it is focused it
owns its keys: Up/k and Down/j scroll, PgUp/PgDn page, Home/End jump to the ends,
and \fB[\fR / \fB]\fR move between sections. Other navigation keys are ignored.
.TP
.B E
On the Debug tab, write a debuginfo bundle into the working directory. The key
never includes the full tree; only \fI\-\-debuginfo-tree\fR can.
.SH SEARCH AND FILTERING
A query is a single line of space-separated clauses combined with AND. A leading
\fB!\fR negates the whole query.
.TP
.B free text
Case-insensitive substring match on the entry name.
.TP
.B glob
A term containing \fB*\fR, \fB?\fR, or \fB[\fR is matched with filepath.Match.
.TP
.B re:PATTERN
Regular-expression match on the entry name.
.TP
.B type:CAT or type:.EXT
Match entries whose broad kind name or specific type id starts with \fICAT\fR
(for example \fIimage\fR, \fIdisk\fR, \fIvdi\fR), or whose extension is \fI.EXT\fR
(for example .go).
.TP
.B size:EXPR
Match by size, using 1024-based suffixes (K, M, G, T). Forms: \fB>10M\fR,
\fB>=1K\fR, \fB<500K\fR, \fB<=2G\fR, and the range \fB1K..2K\fR.
.TP
.B case:
Make matching case-sensitive.
.SH FILES
~/.config/ncdu-next/config.toml
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/1ttyb1tty/ncdu-next/issues
